      "definition_text": "Lufthansa Technik AG (LHT) Design Change Summary (DCS) AQD-23-DCS-09 revision (rev.) 1.",
      "evidence_ids": [
        "EV-004"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "unsafe_condition": {
    "state": "present",
    "raw_reason_text": "Reason: Following a design review, it has been determined that, on aeroplanes affected by this AD, the in-flight entertainment (IFE) control and service box, also named “IFE BinBox”, is installed in an overhead bin in the same compartment with a portable oxygen equipment. This installation is not in compliance with the requirements of EASA CS 25.869(c) and 25.1441(b) and, in case of an ignition mechanism resulting from the IFE BinBox failure (such as a short circuit, electric arcing, etc.) concurrent with oxygen leakage, can lead to an uncontrolled oxygen fire in the cabin. To address this potential unsafe condition, LHT issued the DCS, providing instructions to relocate the IFE BinBox from the overhead stowage compartment (OHSC) above seat row 5, left, to the OHSC above seat row 1, left, minimising possible repercussions to aeroplane adjacent systems and structures in case of IFE BinBox failure. For the reason described above, this AD requires relocation of the IFE BinBox.",
    "observed_events_or_defects": [
      "The IFE BinBox is installed in an overhead bin with portable oxygen equipment."
    ],
    "causes": [
      "Possible IFE BinBox ignition mechanism concurrent with oxygen leakage."
    ],
    "unsafe_conditions": [
      "Installation does not comply with EASA CS 25.869(c) and 25.1441(b)."
    ],
    "potential_consequences": [
      "Uncontrolled oxygen fire in the cabin."
    ],
    "affected_components": [
      "In-flight entertainment control and service box (IFE BinBox)",
      "portable oxygen equipment"
    ],
    "intended_risk_mitigation": [
      "Relocate the IFE BinBox from the row 5 left OHSC to the row 1 left OHSC."
    ],
    "evidence_ids": [
      "EV-005"
    ]
  },
